#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example uses Siemens MF-Tyre/MF-Swift tire model connected with CarSim vehicle model in Simulink in which each of vehicle and tires is represented by a S-Function block.
#
#In order to run, the following extra steps are needed:
#
#1) 	Click "Send to Simulink" button on the CarSim Runs Control screen to open the Simulink model.
#
#2) 	On MATLAB command window, change the current directory to "mathworks" folder under Simcenter tire installation, e.g. \simcenter_tire\mftyre_mfswift-2022.1.1\mathworks\.
#
#3) 	On MATLAB command window, type "mfswift_startup" and hit return key.
#
#4) 	On MATLAB command window, change the current directory to CarSim data root directory, e.g. \CarSim_Data\, or click "Send to Simulink" button on the CarSim Runs Control screen again.
#
#5) 	Click run button on the Simulink model.
#
#
#CarSim imports all tire forces and moments at WC (wheel center) and CTC (central tire contact) from the external tire model; and CarSim exports kinematics variables of location coordinates, velocities, orientation angles, angular speeds, road height/Mu, etc. of each tire to the external tire model.
#
#This Procedure demonstrates a common Double Lane Change handling test.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: CarSim Run Control; { Tire Models (External Software) } MF-Tyre on Simulink: DLC
